  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 224 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nPleasant early October weather is forecast late Friday through early \nnext week, with dry conditions and seasonable temperatures. \nHighs in the 60s and lows in the 40s will be seen. A large \n1027mb surface high will build into the upper Midwest bringing a\ndrier airmass into the CWA. It will be a fantastic weekend for \nany outdoor activities! On Monday, ensemble 850mb temps drop \ninto the 4-8C range and as a result we could see some overnight \nlows dropping into the upper 30s Monday night. \n\nThe next chance of rain will come on Wednesday, as a cold front \nmoves through. Moisture will be limited as noted by 1000-500mb RH \nprogs and this could end up just bringing an increase in clouds. \nThis would be good news for farmers wanting their fields to dry out \nto start planning their harvest.",
